.TH PAPERWEIGHT\-SETTINGS 1 "2026-11-08" "paperweight-skel 0.2.87" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paperweight\-settings \- PaperweightOS settings menu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperweight\-settings
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paperweight\-settings
opens a
.BR wofi (1)
menu of system settings tools and runs the one you pick.
It is bound to
.B Super+,
(\fB$mod+comma\fR) and also opens with a right\-click on the PaperweightOS
logo in the bar.
.PP
PaperweightOS gives a direct key only to things used every day.
Settings that are changed rarely, such as the theme or wallpaper, live in
this menu instead.
.PP
With the standard packages installed, the menu lists:
.TP
.B Theme
.BR paperweight\-theme (1)
.TQ
.B Wallpaper
.BR paperweight\-wallpaper (1)
(from paperweight\-wallpapers)
.TQ
.B Network
.BR paperweight\-network (1)
.TQ
.B Sound
.BR pavucontrol (1)
.TQ
.B Password setup
.BR paperweight\-secrets\-init (1)
in a terminal (from paperweight\-secrets)
.TQ
.B Keybindings
.BR paperweight\-keys (1)
.TQ
.B Power
.BR wlogout (1)
.SH ENTRY FILES
Each entry is a small file in a
.I settings.d
directory.
Packages ship theirs in
.IR /usr/share/paperweight\-os/settings.d/ ;
yours go in
.IR ~/.config/paperweight\-os/settings.d/ .
A file holds two lines:
.PP
.RS
.nf
Name=Theme
Exec=paperweight\-theme
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Exec
is run with
.BR sh (1),
so it may use quoting, pipes and
.BR ; .
.PP
Name files
.IR NN\-name ,
where
.I NN
is a number that sets the position in the menu.
A file in your directory with the same name as a shipped one replaces it,
and an empty file with that name hides the entry.
For example, to hide Sound:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mkdir \-p ~/.config/paperweight\-os/settings.d
: > ~/.config/paperweight\-os/settings.d/40\-sound
.fi
.RE
.PP
Entries are read each time the menu opens, so changes apply immediately.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/paperweight\-os/settings.d/
Entries shipped by packages.
.TP
.I ~/.config/paperweight\-os/settings.d/
Your own entries and overrides
(\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/paperweight\-os/settings.d/\fR if set).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paperweight\-keys (1),
.BR paperweight\-theme (1),
.BR paperweight\-network (1),
.BR wofi (1)
